  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CAFOD Managed Programme - CAFOD funding - Year 1</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall goal of this project is to contribute to the improvement of the health status of poor people living in rural areas of northern Nigeria. The project aims to strengthen Catholic-Church health structures, focusing in particular on PHC facilities, in order to enable them to provide high quality, sustainable health care services that meet the needs of poor rural communities in 19 states and the Federal Capital Territory. The project will work with some of the most underserved communities in Northern Nigeria to ensure a more equal access to health facilities and will focus on the most vulnerable sectors of the communities including children, women, and people living with HIV/AIDS (PLWHAs).</narrative>
  </description>
